{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives."}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"title":"HTTPDestination","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination.swift#L85","fileName":"HTTPDestination.swift"},"role":"symbol"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:transport:encoder:backoff:clock:now:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/Destination-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","text":"HTTPTransport","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","text":"BatchEncoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The requests the encoder splits each batch into (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"), in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order the delivery hands batches over, each request sent only once the previous one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered or dropped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the request’s first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record, then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names are the instrument’s: ","type":"text"},{"code":"traceparent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"tracestate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NoOpInstrument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a request may hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, where a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" writes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType"},{"text":", whatever a configured","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field or the instrument wrote.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the request’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request the transport can never send ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an "},{"code":"http","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Retry-After"},{"type":"text","text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the request, and it isn’t sent again. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch’s later requests are still sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request with a deadline (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","isActive":true},{"text":") is sent only while the destination’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wall clock reads that time or earlier, checked before every attempt, the first included, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again when an attempt fails. One still undelivered once it has passed isn’t sent again, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is reported without waiting out a backoff, so a vendor that would misdate or ignore records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that old never receives them. The whole request is dropped, its younger records too; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch’s later requests are still sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"text":") may have arrived before. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"text":" is the one it was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch of several requests is acknowledged only once every request is delivered or dropped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A delivery cancelled, or an app stopped, after some of its requests arrived hands the whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch over again, so those requests are sent again too: a server that keeps one copy per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record identifier absorbs them. The records the encoder leaves out are then reported again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A request the endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rejects, that can’t be sent or that passed its deadline, a batch the encoder can’t encode, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a record the encoder leaves out of its requests are dropped: logged at error level and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported on ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"level.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns without logging or reporting it, or sending the batch’s later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests. A request whose wait before the next attempt throws something other than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CancellationError"},{"text":" (a custom clock’s failure) is given up on, logged at error level but not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported, and the batch’s next request is sent.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which drops its oldest batch when full and reports it on the delivery’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"bufferDropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"With a store, a dropped batch’s records aren’t lost: once this destination has caught up, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery reads them back from the store and hands them to it again, in the same run, so they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are sent once the endpoint answers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Without a store, the records of a dropped batch are lost.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"generated":true,"title":"Sending batches"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/receive(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Sends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"batch"},{"text":" to the endpoint, as the requests its encoder splits it into, one after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"another; sends each again after each transient failure, and returns once every one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered or dropped, or the delivery is cancelled.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/receive(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"receive"},{"kind":"text","text":"(["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EventRecord"},{"kind":"text","text":"]) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"title":"receive(_:)"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:now:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/init(endpoint:headerfields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:now:)","title":"init(endpoint:headerFields:instrument:encoder:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession.shared","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", encoded by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"encoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the